Found by mcp-hub-worker during k42. The background warm-up calls start_p on a failed placeholder (_broken_upstream) of a stdio/http/docker/fork entry, which logs the build error a second time.

2026-11-05 23:48 Fix: MCP::Hub::_warm_upstream returns early for an upstream whose state is 'failed' — at warm time that is only a placeholder (_broken_upstream): it has nothing to fetch, and its start would only reject with the build error that was logged when it was built. Regression test t/hub.t 'the build error of a placeholder is logged once': a {class => 'No::Such::Forked::Class', hub => {fork => true}} entry with a captured Mojo::Log; exactly one line contains the error, and it is the 'failed to build upstream broken:' one. Red verified against a lib copy without the guard (two lines: the build error plus 'upstream broken: cannot load class …').

